==Trivia==
*Masked Cat is likely a reference to [[wikipedia:The Mask of Zorro|The Mask of Zorro]] as Masked Cat's translated Japanese name, Mask of Cat, is similar to the film's name. The masks worn by Zorro and the Cat are also designed similarly and both leave the mouth and eyes uncovered. Additionally, in [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]], Masked Cat's description stated that it stole the mask from Harrison, which is likely a nod to the film's Harrison Love.
*[[Gamatoto Expedition|Gamatoto]] is mentioned in Masked Cat's description, even though he wasn't implemented at that point yet.
**Masked Cat's description didn't mention Gamatoto in [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]], making it possible that the reference was only added once Gamatoto was.
*This Cat unit is the first to reference Gamatoto, the second being [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]].
*One of the skins in [[Battle Cats Quest]] is named Masked Cat, although that cat bears no real resemblance to this one.
*Not counting [[:Category:Collaboration Event Cats|Collaboration Cats]], [[Capsule Cat (Special Cat)|Capsule Cat]] and Masked Cat are tied for the oldest existing Special Cats without [[True Form]]s.

